>> title: Egg Fried Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, eggs, chinese, wok, quick
>> counters: Takeout Counter, Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: fried rice, house fried rice, chow fan, 炒饭
>> pairs-with: red-braised-pork-belly
>> servings: 4
>> time: 20 min

>> step: beat
Beat @eggs{4%large} with @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}.

>> step: scramble 1 min
Scramble @&(~1)eggs{} in @peanut oil{2%Tbs} in a hot #wok{} until just set, ~{1%min}, breaking them into curds.

>> step: stir-fry 3 min
Stir-fry @&(~1)eggs{} with @cold cooked jasmine rice{4%cups}(600 g; day-old) over high heat for ~{3%min}, pressing out the clumps.

>> step: toss
Toss @&(~1)rice{} with @soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{1%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: fold in
Fold @scallions{4}(thinly sliced) and @frozen peas{1/2%cup}(70 g; thawed) into @&(~1)rice{}.
